    docs(CF-151): measure the node's credential, not the control host's key
    
    The pre-fix row cited the control-host command
    HERMES_PYTHON_BIN=python3.12 scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check as the
    contradiction for the node credential state; on a keyed control host that gate
    reads the host's own ~/.hermes/.env and prints PASS inference_key (five gate
    rows, HERMES: FAIL (1) on port, rc 1), the opposite of the row's **missing**
    state. The row now scopes the contradiction to the node: the gate failing
    inside the node via ~/node-scripts/project-node.sh --check --project <p>,
    whose layer 20 echoes scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh --check reading the
    node's $HOME/.hermes/.env, with the control-host run labelled as this host's
    own key only.
    
    Binds the rewording with tests/selftest.sh section 37
    (cf151-node-credential-scope): it refuses the verbatim pre-fix row bytes and
    requires the control-host label plus a node-scoped measurement or an explicit
    node-state statement. RED at authoring: SELFTEST: FAIL (1) against the
    pre-fix README (baseline 276b0b0).
